    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Vision work-up at intake: visual acuity with and without pinhole, pupils, red reflex and a functional history (faces, reading signs, driving, glare, falls); HbA1c for diabetic retinopathy risk; urgent eye care for any sudden loss, pain or redness. Guideline: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and rheumatoid arthritis/osteoarthritis monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Ophthalmology consultation (cataract) for a comprehensive dilated eye examination, intraocular pressure and macular OCT, the cause of the vision loss, and surgical candidacy. Guideline: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and rheumatoid arthritis/osteoarthritis monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Falls and low vision: brighter lighting on the porch and stairs, contrast tape on step edges, a second handrail, night lights; no driving until vision meets the state standard. Guideline: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024) [S]</item><item>Low back pain: lumbar X-ray at intake to look for a retained fragment at the old wound (and to clear any later MRI); reassurance and staying active; physical therapy with exercise and motor control training, then a home program, with heat; no opioids, no muscle relaxants; a short course of an oral anti-inflammatory only if exercise is not enough. Guideline: Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2017) [S]</item><item>Goiter: TSH and free T4; thyroid ultrasound with the sonographic pattern of each nodule; fine-needle aspiration only for a nodule that meets size and pattern thresholds; follow-up ultrasound at an interval set by the findings; return for trouble swallowing or breathing, voice change or rapid growth. Guideline: 2015 American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer (2015) [S]</item><item>Knees: quadriceps strengthening, walking and tai chi; topical diclofenac; a stick in the outside hand on slopes. Guideline: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, cataract and rheumatoid arthritis/osteoarthritis monographs (2026) [S]</item><item>Instructions by ear: every plan explained aloud with teach-back, medicine schedules recorded as voice reminders and shown by demonstration, and large-print copies for his household. Guideline: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021) [S]</item></list></text>

